-   entry .inspectable   renders a stroke by its case name with its fields, `MoveTo(Point(x:0.0F ╱ y:0.0F))`
-       Spelt out rather than derived, since the path-data form (`A 3.0 4.0 0.0 1 0 …`) drops
-       the case names a reader is matching against the source.
-   entry .encodable   a stroke as its path-data text, as `stroke.encode`
-       `M x y`, `m dx dy`, `L x y`, `l dx dy` (or `h dx` / `v dy` when the shift is along one
-       axis), `C c1, c2, p` / `S c2, p`, `Q c1, p` / `T p`, their lowercase relative forms,
-       `A rx ry angle large sweep p` with the flags as `1` or `0`, and `Z`. The relative arc
-       is written with `A` and its shift's components, as the source has it.
